{
    desc => ':set theme=dark switches from default to dark theme',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/set_theme_dark`

Tests that `:set theme=dark` applies the dark color scheme at runtime,
changing the editor background to a dark tone (#1E1E1E) and adjusting
all foreground and syntax colors accordingly.

Starts from the default (light) theme so the transition is visible.

Ex: `:set theme=dark`

- **set_theme_dark_light_initial.png**: Default light theme with white
  background, dark text, and standard syntax colors.
- **set_theme_dark_applied.png**: Dark theme active with dark background,
  light text, and dark-appropriate syntax highlighting colors.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->editor->set_theme('default');
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('light_initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('set theme=dark');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('applied');
    },
}
__DATA__
# Theme switch test
Hello, World!
my $x = 42;
print "dark mode\n";
